    "title": "HTTP Caching: Freshness and Revalidation",
    "kind": "live",
    "rootId": "root",
    "explorations": {
      "root": {
        "id": "root",
        "title": "HTTP Caching: Freshness and Revalidation",
        "summary": "Explains browser HTTP cache reuse: fresh responses from Cache-Control max-age are used directly; stale or no-cache responses are revalidated with ETag/If-None-Match, where 304 means reuse cache.",
        "parentId": null,
        "source": null,
        "messages": [
          {
            "id": "question-smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8",
            "role": "user",
            "requestId": "smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8",
            "source": null,
            "sections": [
              {
                "id": "prompt-smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8",
                "title": "",
                "body": "Explain how a browser decides whether to use a cached HTTP response. Cover freshness, Cache-Control, ETag revalidation, and one small example."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "answer-smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8",
            "role": "assistant",
            "requestId": "smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8",
            "source": null,
            "routing": {
              "decision": "continue",
              "reason": "First answer in this conversation, so it continues the current topic."
            },
            "model": "muse-spark-1.3",
            "context": {
              "fullIds": [
                "root"
              ],
              "summaryIds": [],
              "truncated": false
            },
            "sections": [
              {
                "id": "section-smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8-0",
                "title": "Freshness first, revalidation second",
                "body": "When a browser needs a resource it has seen before, it checks its HTTP cache in this order:\n\n**1. Freshness:** Can it reuse the stored response immediately?\n- `Cache-Control: max-age=3600` means reuse for up to 3600 seconds without contacting the server.\n- `Cache-Control: no-cache` means always check with server first.\n- `Cache-Control: no-store` means do not cache at all.\n- `Expires` is the older alternative to `max-age`.\n\nIf fresh, the browser uses it with no network request.\n\n**2. Revalidation:** If stale or `no-cache`, ask the server if the copy is still valid.\n- Server previously sent `ETag: \"abc123\"` or `Last-Modified`.\n- Browser sends conditional request: `If-None-Match: \"abc123\"` or `If-Modified-Since`.\n- Server replies `304 Not Modified` with no body -> browser reuses cache.\n- Server replies `200 OK` with new body -> browser replaces cache."
              },
              {
                "id": "section-smoke-faeb4636-350f-483a-bde8-c624fdbb54a8-1",
                "title": "Small example",
                "body": "1. Browser requests `/logo.png`.\n2. Server responds:\n```http\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nCache-Control: max-age=60\nETag: \"v1\"\n```\n3. Request within 60s: fresh, browser uses cache, no request sent.\n4. Request after 60s: stale, browser sends:\n```http\nGET /logo.png\nIf-None-Match: \"v1\"\n```\n5. If unchanged, server sends `304 Not Modified` and browser reuses cached file. If changed, server sends `200 OK` with new `ETag`."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "position": [
          0,
